      "title": "Quantum computer learns to fix itself while running",
      "summary": "Researchers from Rutgers, IBM and partner institutions showed a quantum computer can check what is happening inside it and respond mid-run, repeatedly resetting parts of the system to bring chaotic behavior under control. This is a step toward machines that correct their own mistakes, which is the main barrier to useful quantum computing. It is still a lab demonstration, and large, reliable error-corrected machines remain well off.",
